        "id": 1072905
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T10:25:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why disabled caches too?\n\nA node with `memoryLimit \u003d 0` may not have the entry locally, but a peer may still have it cached.\nSo we still need to send the invalidation so the peer can remove its stale entry.\n\n\u003e There isn\u0027t such a thing as a disabled cache. Even when setting the max size to zero, entries are created and then immediately expire.\n\nYou\u0027re right; I rephrased this to \"including caches with memoryLimit \u003d 0\".",
      "parentUuid": "7d5d7883_5b757ae1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 56
      },
